KNOWNBUG: [dcl.struct.bind]/4 -- when std::tuple_size<E> is complete, a
structured binding must bind each name to get<i>(e), not to the i-th data
member.  CBMC decomposes by data member, which gives the wrong elements for a
tuple-like type whose data-member order differs from its get<i> order (e.g.
std::tuple).  This is why `auto [a,b] = std::tuple<int,long>(1,2)` binds b
incorrectly.  Flip to CORE once the get-protocol is implemented.
